From 24f7ee3b08a8813bfda96cc5c1f95d37e89a4546 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:58:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] GFS_phys_time_vary: build Noah-MP snow layers from the
 land snow with frac_grid

At a cold start fv3atm derives the land snow weasdl = weasd/(landfrac +
fice*(1-landfrac)) and noahmpdrv is handed weasdl, but GFS_phys_time_vary_init
built Noah-MP's snow layers (snicexy) from the cell-mean composite weasd and
snowd. On its first step Noah-MP rebuilds its snow total from the layers, so
coastal and glacier land lost weasdl - weasd at once.

Use weasdl and snodl in the Noah-MP initialisation block.

Where the initial state has snow depth but no snow water (sheleg = 0,
snwdph > 0), no layers are built. Dividing by a small land fraction can turn
such a depth into enough land snow for layers (0.058 mm cell-mean -> 15 cm
at landfrac 3.9e-4 in the coupled regression cases' initial state), and
layers with no ice have zero heat capacity: a divide by zero in Noah-MP's
energy routine on the first step. develop builds no layers there either.

Measured with in-model meters (C96 control_p8_ugwpv1, frac_grid): the first
step removed 0.29 kg/m2 of snow as a global mean (about 1 kg/m2 per unit land
area, in ~3700 coastal snowy columns and the glacier margins). With the fix
Noah-MP's water check is 0 on the first step.

Adapted to production/AQM.v7 (67d069ad6) from ufs/dev c7dc705. This branch's glacier branch floors weasd at 0.1 mm instead of setting 600 mm; that floor now acts on weasdl, as the 600 mm override does on ufs/dev. Dummy declared allocatable like its neighbours in this file.
